
WindowExplorer: Not a game.
Release 2 / Serial number 110119 / Inform v6.32, compiler options S
Interpreter version 0.3.0 / VM 3.1.3 / game file format 3.0.0

A voice booooms out: Welcome to the test chamber.

Type "help" to repeat this message, "quit"/"exit"/"return" to exit, or one of the following:

  "windows": List all open windows.
  "size": Show the sizes of all open windows.
  "open PARAMS": Open a second window. PARAMS can include any of left/right/top/bottom, fixed/proportional, border/noborder, grid/buffer/blank/graphic, and a (numeric) size.
  "close": Close the second window.
  "arrange PARAMS": Change the second window arrangement. The PARAMS are the same as above. (Note: not all parameters are legal, so you can cause a Glk error with this command.)
  "getline": Request line input in the second window.
  "dropline": Cancel line input in the second window.
  "echoline NUM": Begin/end line-input echoing in the second window.
  "echo": Begin echoing all output from the first window to the second window. (Causes a Glk error if mixed with "getline".)
  "streams": List all open streams.
  "styles": Display a sample line of each text style.
  "dialog MODE": Open a file-selection dialog.
  "timer NUM": Start (or stop) a timer, which fires every NUM seconds (default 1).
  "poll": Poll for upcoming events. (There will normally not be any.)
  "link": Display some clickable hyperlinks.

